From: Atomic Chat <noreply@atomic.chat>
Subject: [PATCH] server: keep serving the loaded model in single-model mode

Atomic Chat's core starts mlx-server with MLX_VLM_SINGLE_MODEL=1 and loads
exactly one model; it never hot-swaps. Clients put arbitrary labels in the
request's `model` field (a catalog id, a repo short name), and upstream treats
any label that differs from the cached one as a new model: it unloads the loaded
one and tries to fetch the label from Hugging Face, which fails (401 for a
private or non-existent repo) and breaks the session. With
MLX_VLM_SINGLE_MODEL=1 the requested label is ignored and the model cached in
the request's cache group keeps serving.

Used by: atomic-chat-core src/runtime/mlx/runtime.ts (sets the variable); the
core forwards the request body as is, with its own model id in `model`.
Released cores get every new build (the MLX manifest has no
min_core_version), so the core cannot stop relying on it: keep it until
upstream has an equivalent switch that every core in use already sets.
Guarded by atomic/tests/test_patches.py::test_single_model_*.

diff --git a/mlx_vlm/server/app.py b/mlx_vlm/server/app.py
index ace5667c..f4357aa0 100644
--- a/mlx_vlm/server/app.py
+++ b/mlx_vlm/server/app.py
@@ -694,6 +694,32 @@ def get_cached_model(
             cached_cache["config"],
         )
 
+    # Atomic-Chat fork addition: in single-model mode the server is launched
+    # by a desktop app that pre-loads exactly one model and never expects
+    # hot-swap. Clients in the wild pass arbitrary labels (model_id, repo
+    # short-name, etc.) in the `model` field of the request body — without
+    # this guard we would unload and try to fetch them from HF, which 401s
+    # for non-existent / private repos and breaks the whole session. When
+    # `MLX_VLM_SINGLE_MODEL=1` is set, ignore the requested label and keep
+    # serving the model already cached in this cache group. Scoped to the
+    # current `cache_group` so it composes with upstream's per-group cache
+    # registry (text / audio / image); the desktop only drives text.
+    if os.environ.get("MLX_VLM_SINGLE_MODEL") == "1" and cached_cache:
+        cached_key = cached_cache.get("cache_key")
+        cached_path = cached_key[0] if cached_key else None
+        print(
+            f"Single-model mode: ignoring requested '{model_path}', "
+            f"serving cached '{cached_path}'."
+        )
+        if cache_group == "text_generation":
+            runtime.response_generator = cached_cache.get("response_generator")
+            runtime.apc_manager = cached_cache.get("apc_manager")
+        return (
+            cached_cache["model"],
+            cached_cache["processor"],
+            cached_cache["config"],
+        )
+
     # If this kind has a different model cached, clear only that cache group.
     if cached_cache:
         logger.info("New %s model requested; clearing its existing cache.", cache_group)
